cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this protocol or the derived statistics, please cite it as below."
title: "Matrix stiffness x neuropathic pain: prospectively specified reanalysis of GSE98547, GSE111216 and GSE261676"
abstract: >-
  A prospectively specified reanalysis testing whether a matrix-stiffness-responsive,
  YAP/TAZ-dependent transcriptional programme (derived from GSE98547 in HEK293A) is
  activated in dorsal root ganglion and spinal cord after nerve injury or inflammation.
  The HEK293A-derived signature does not transfer: Stage A is uninformative (blood
  negative control equally non-significant, BH q = 0.409) and Stage B shows a bounded,
  sensitivity-validated null for HD_up (Hedges g = 0.219, P = 0.80) against a detected
  positive control (g = 3.85, P = 0.0286). Crucially, five independent, literature-sourced
  ECM/mechanotransduction gene sets retain tissue specificity in pain transcriptomes
  (4/5 DRG > blood; only the YAP/TAZ-class set fails, SI = 0.44), so the projection
  failure is signature- and cell-type-specific rather than a universal property of
  stiffness-program projection.
